//      hard mask leaves only one token choice. The `!`-loop then exhausts the budget.
//   2. EOS emitted inside an open span causes the span to never close.
//   3. 24 wrong answers: semantically wrong (missing int(), wrong formula). Better
//      guidance to emphasize int() and prohibited tokens (^, =, !).
//
// Fix 1 — span length cap: Before each constrained step, check if
//   |currentConstrainedOut| >= maxSpanLength (35). If so, call CloseSpanWithinBudget
//   with all remaining budget. CloseSpanWithinBudget is dead-end-aware and rolls
//   back to the last complete prefix, cutting off any !-loop after at most 35 tokens.
//
// Fix 2 — EOS salvage: When SafeRepetitionPenaltyStep returns eosToken inside a
//   span, call CloseSpanWithinBudget with the remaining budget to close the span
//   before breaking, rather than leaving it unclosed.
//
// Kept from attempt 2:
//   - SafeRepetitionPenaltyStep(4.0) for normal constrained steps.
//   - closeReserve=80 (proven effective in best attempt).
//   - Free-generation + RenderedEndsWith detection for span entry.
//   - Final cleanup call to CloseSpanWithinBudget.
// CSD_RATIONALE_END
// CSD_PROOF_SKETCH_BEGIN
// Invariant 1 — parser_validity:
//   insideConstrainedOut ==> parser.IsValidPrefix(currentConstrainedOut)
//
